      "statement": "Notebook clean-state hygiene is enforced by scripts/check_notebooks.py: dirty_cells() parses each notebook's JSON and flags code cells with non-empty outputs or non-null execution_count; main() checks the notebooks passed as arguments (or all notebooks/**/*.ipynb when none are given), prints the offending cell indices, and returns 1 with the hint 'uv run nbstripout <notebook.ipynb>' (not a make target) when any are dirty, otherwise returns 0. It never modifies notebooks.",
